# v0.8.2 PATCH — `loam release` accepts scope-descriptive plan-doc paths

2026-05-13. Sealed local; awaiting dispatcher dogfood publish per
ASK-FIRST. v0.8.2 closes a defect surfaced by the
`feedback_version_numbers_at_release_time` convention shift
(captured 2026-05-13): plan-doc filenames are now scope-descriptive
(the slug describes the work, no version pre-baked) and version
derives at release-time from `(current_published, class)`. The
v0.6.0 release-CLI gates infer their input paths from the version
slug, so the first downstream consumer of the new convention (the
paper publish at `docs/plans/odd-paper-methodology-publish.md`)
can't pass `loam release` gates without a fix.

The fix is a single new flag — `--plan-doc <path>` — on
`loam release` that overrides path inference for two gates:

- `check_acs_verified` reads the named plan-doc directly when the
  flag is provided (skipping the version-slug glob lookup).
- `check_hard_smoke` reads `docs/experiments/<plan-doc-stem>-hard-smoke.md`
  when the flag is provided (stem extraction via `Path.stem`).

Flag-absent behaviour is preserved verbatim: every existing
`loam release <version>` invocation against a version-named
plan-doc continues to work. 4 new tests at
`framework/tools/loam/tests/test_AC_SDPD_plan_doc_flag.py` cover
the flag-acceptance + flag-honoring + RED-with-hint surfaces.
Backward-compat verified by existing
`test_AC_V060_2_pre_publish_gates.py` test suite passing
unmodified.

AC.SDPD.4 outcome-altitude dogfood: invoked
`loam release v0.9.0 --plan-doc docs/plans/odd-paper-methodology-publish.md
--dry-run` against the live paper-publish artefacts (v0.9.0
